{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n\nEvery COMPLETION_VERDICT sidecar is emitted with `material=None` — `completion_sidecar.emit(result, material=None, repo_root=repo_root)` at `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py:405`, with the comment at `:754` noting no fingerprint is computed on this path. Measured on the live store: 0 of the most recent 300 COMPLETION_VERDICT sidecars (216 PASS / 59 FAIL / 23 no-verdict / 2 ERROR) carry any material/material_fingerprint field.\n\n## Consequence (why this is worth fixing)\n\nA FAIL followed by a PASS on the same `verified_at_sha` cannot be attributed: verifier inputs include ticket comments and prefetched evidence, which change without a code commit, so \"no commit in between\" does not mean \"same inputs.\" This makes the completion gate's precision unmeasurable from its own records (an analysis this week mis-derived an \"80–84% FP\" figure from exactly this gap), and it means completion attestations cannot support the stale-material currency discipline that plan-review attestations already have.\n\nNote: the `material=None` is deliberate per the code's own comment — this ticket treats the capability gap as the defect (operator-directed filing, 2026-08-31). Formula/prompt version stamping in the same record would make longitudinal gate analysis version-aware (pass-3 blocking formulas have changed over time, so unversioned sidecars conflate formula eras).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] COMPLETION_VERDICT sidecars (PASS, FAIL, ERROR alike) record a material fingerprint over the verifier's actual inputs (ticket material as pinned for the run: description/ACs/comments snapshot + evidence set identifiers), reusing the existing plan-review fingerprint machinery where applicable rather than inventing a new scheme.\n- [ ] Sidecars record the verifier formula/prompt version identifier alongside the fingerprint.\n- [ ] Existing sidecars are untouched (no backfill); consumers treat absent material as \"unknown era\".\n- [ ] A regression test asserts a FAIL sidecar carries a non-null fingerprint and version.\n\n## File impact\n\nTo be confirmed at investigation (bugs do not pre-declare impact): expected `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py`, `src/rebar/llm/completion_sidecar.py` (or equivalent emitter), one test module.\n\n## Fix plan (2026-08-31, revised after plan-review BLOCK)\n\n### Root cause\n\nThe completion verifier already computes/pins input identity before close publication, but close-time and standalone sidecar emitters pass `material=None`, and `completion_sidecar.build_payload` serializes only that explicit argument. Atomic PASS also calls `build_payload` directly. The sidecar therefore drops the verifier-input identity it already has. Completion ERROR records in the same `COMPLETION_VERDICT` stream also lack a version/fingerprint stamp.\n\n### Required fingerprint shape\n\nFor PASS/FAIL verdict sidecars, `material_fingerprint` will be a deterministic sha256-16 over a JSON object named `completion_verifier_material_v1` containing:\n\n1. `plan_material_fingerprint`: the existing plan-review material fingerprint already computed by `current_material_fingerprint`/`pass1.material_fingerprint` and carried on the verifier result;\n2. `completion_read_basis`: the pinned `completion_read_basis` identifiers (`code_oid`, `tickets_oid`, `receipt_digest`, `run_id`) when present. The receipt digest is mandatory for the pinned close path because it covers the ticket/comments snapshot actually consulted;\n3. `prefetch_manifest`: the evidence-set identifiers already embedded in the verifier context's `PRE-LOAD MANIFEST` (`path` + `mode`) when present.\n\nFallbacks are explicit and era-visible: if a legacy/local caller has no completion read basis, the fingerprint falls back to the existing plan material fingerprint plus a `basis_unavailable` marker, never to `None` for an otherwise materialized ticket. If no ticket material can be computed at all, the sidecar remains best-effort/unknown rather than changing the gate result.\n\nFor completion `gate_error_v1` ERROR sidecars, no pinned verdict result may exist. Those records will carry the same version stamp and the best available material identity: the existing current material fingerprint plus an `error_unpinned` marker. This is intentionally not comparable to the pinned PASS/FAIL composite, and the record will expose that via `material_basis: \"error_unpinned\"`.\n\n### Required version shape\n\nEach new completion sidecar will carry a nested `verifier_version` object:\n\n- `prompt_id`: `completion-verifier`\n- `prompt_content_sha256`: git-canonical content hash from the prompt library (`prompt_content_hash(canonical_prompt_text(...))`)\n- `formula_version`: the gate-code version string from `signing.gate_code_version()`\n\nThis reuses existing prompt and gate-version machinery instead of a new registry. Old records without this object are the unknown era.\n\n### Scope / file impact\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/completion_sidecar.py`: derive/stamp PASS/FAIL `material_fingerprint`, `material_basis`, and `verifier_version` in the shared builder/emitter.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/completion_bundle.py`: atomic PASS direct `build_payload` caller; ensure the enriched payload remains compatible with bundle/signing behavior.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py`: update stale material-less comment; outcome and failure swallowing unchanged.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py`: standalone `verify-completion` recording remains outcome-compatible while shared emitter enriches records.\n- `src/rebar/llm/gate_error_sidecar.py`: stamp completion ERROR records with best-effort `material_fingerprint`, `material_basis`, and `verifier_version` without changing error propagation.\n- `tests/unit/test_completion_sidecar_material_balding.py`: RED/GREEN tests for FAIL sidecar fingerprint+version, PASS/direct builder coverage, ERROR payload coverage, and old-record absence tolerance.\n\n### Verification plan\n\n1. RED first: add the FAIL-sidecar regression test and run only it; it must fail because current `completion_sidecar.emit(... material=None ...)` writes `material_fingerprint: null` and no `verifier_version`.\n2. GREEN: implement record enrichment only; run the new test module and existing focused sidecar/atomic-close tests.\n3. Mutation-teeth: in a sandbox, reintroduce the omission by making the builder ignore verdict material again; the held-out FAIL test must return to RED, then restore the fix.\n4. Safety: confirm emitted verdict strings, signability, close blocking, and best-effort swallowing are unchanged; only sidecar payload fields are additive/filled.\n\n### Acceptance criteria mapping\n\n- AC1: PASS/FAIL sidecars fingerprint the pinned verifier inputs via existing plan material plus completion read-basis receipt digest and prefetch identifiers. ERROR sidecars carry best available current material and mark the unpinned basis.\n- AC2: `verifier_version` records prompt id, prompt content hash, and formula/gate-code version.\n- AC3: No backfill, prune, or reader rejection change; absent fields remain accepted as unknown-era records.\n- AC4: The RED→GREEN FAIL sidecar test asserts non-null fingerprint and version.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788234524128444001,"uuid":"60685145-e29c-4cd6-931f-a3dd8faccf1a"}